            <ArticleTitle>An alternative method of prosthetic mitral valve implantation in the presence of extensive calcification.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>199-201</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Annular calcifications carry some technical difficulties for success in conventional valve surgery. In this paper we present an easy alternative mitral valve replacement method applied for a patient with a heavily calcified mitral annulus. Excision of both leaflets and partial resection of the annular calcification with an ultrasonic dissector allowed the intra-atrial insertion of a 33-mm Omnicarbon monoleaflet prosthetic valve through a smaller opening of the left posterior atrium. The technical difficulties in inserting a prosthetic valve in a patient with a heavily calcified mitral annulus are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
